// ---------------- GABA-A plasticity: the slow change detector -------------
TAU_M       : 1.0   : ALLO exposure-memory time constant (d)
TAU_MP      : 1.0   : Progestogen-tone memory time constant (d)
TAU_D       : 5.0   : Delta-subunit time constant (d)
TAU_A4      : 1.2   : Alpha4-subunit time constant (d)
HD          : 1.25  : Maximum delta upregulation
KD          : 3.0   : ALLO for half-maximal delta upregulation (nM)
HA          : 2.20  : Maximum alpha4 upregulation
KA          : 0.55  : Change signal for half-maximal alpha4 upregulation
KRISE       : 0.55  : Weight of a RISING signal relative to a falling one
W_PROG      : 0.85  : Weight of progestogen-tone change relative to ALLO
GAMMA_D     : -0.35 : Delta gain — NEGATIVE = tolerance (controls -0.05)
GAMMA_A4    : 1.50  : Alpha4 gain — POSITIVE = sensitisation (controls 0.25)
// ---------------- inverted-U transduction ---------------------------------
KP          : 5.0   : Neurosteroid load at the response PEAK (nM) — the disease parameter (controls 13)
MONOTONE    : 0     : 1 = replace the inverted U with a level detector
RATE_OFF    : 0     : 1 = disable every rate/withdrawal detector
